1
00:00:00,170 --> 00:00:03,570
In 1925, a man sold the Eiffel Tower.

2
00:00:03,570 --> 00:00:04,700
He didn't own it.

3
00:00:04,940 --> 00:00:06,890
Paris 1925.

4
00:00:06,890 --> 00:00:09,050
The tower is rusting and expensive to keep

5
00:00:09,110 --> 00:00:09,900
standing.

6
00:00:10,140 --> 00:00:12,400
Victor Lustig reads that in a newspaper

7
00:00:12,400 --> 00:00:14,110
and sees an opportunity.

8
00:00:14,110 --> 00:00:16,350
He forges government letterhead and

9
00:00:16,350 --> 00:00:18,410
invites six scrap dealers to a secret

10
00:00:18,410 --> 00:00:20,630
meeting at a luxury hotel.

11
00:00:20,630 --> 00:00:23,380
The city, he says, is quietly selling the

12
00:00:23,380 --> 00:00:25,890
tower for scrap, seven thousand tons of

13
00:00:25,890 --> 00:00:27,900
iron, and nobody can know.

14
00:00:27,900 --> 00:00:30,450
One dealer Andre Poisson pays, Lustig

15
00:00:30,450 --> 00:00:33,170
takes the money and catches the next train

16
00:00:33,170 --> 00:00:33,910
to Vienna.

17
00:00:33,910 --> 00:00:36,200
And Poisson never calls the police.

18
00:00:36,200 --> 00:00:37,800
He's too embarrassed.

19
00:00:37,800 --> 00:00:40,060
So a month later Lustig comes back and

20
00:00:40,060 --> 00:00:42,010
tries to sell the tower again.

21
00:00:42,330 --> 00:00:43,700
Would you have fallen for it?

22
00:00:43,700 --> 00:00:45,600
Follow for more true stories.
